<title>UK: Halifax shoots to No.8 in UK's FTSE 100.</title>
<headline>Halifax shoots to No.8 in UK's FTSE 100.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's biggest mortgage lender, Halifax Plc, on Monday became the eighth largest listed company on its debut to the London Stock Exchange (LSE).</p>
<p>Halifax, which started its first day of trading on the LSE at 774-1/2p, was quoted at 745p by 1000 GMT, valuing the company at around 18.7 billion stg.</p>
<p>The top 10 shares on the LSE in terms of market capitalisation are as follows:</p>
<p> Company				     Market Cap(stg)</p>
<p> 1. HSBC Holdings Plc		    49.94 billion</p>
<p> 2. Glaxo Wellcome Plc		   43.74 billion</p>
<p> 3. British Petroleum Co Plc	   41.34 billion</p>
<p> 4. Shell Transport &amp; Trading Co Plc 40.13 billion</p>
<p> 5. Lloyds TSB Group Plc		 33.15 billion</p>
<p> 6. SmithKline Beecham Plc	     29.15 billion</p>
<p> 7. British Telecommunications Plc   28.03 billion</p>
<p> 8. Halifax Plc			    18.70 billion</p>
<p> 9. Barclays Plc			   18.12 billion</p>
<p> 10.Zeneca Group Plc		     17.68 billion</p>
<p>(Note: Market cap based on closing prices on May 30, 1997. Source Reuters Securities 3000.)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
